SUMMARY:Deadline 12:00 Hong Kong time: Hong Kong PhD Fellowship Scheme 2027
 /28 (HKD 344\,400 a year for up to three years\; 400 fellowships\, practic
 e-led art PhDs included)
DESCRIPTION:Closes 01 Dec 2026 at 12:00 Hong Kong time.\n\nThe Hong Kong Ph
 D Fellowship Scheme\, run by the Research Grants Council\, funds around 40
 0 new full-time PhD students a year at eight Hong Kong universities\, in a
 ny discipline\, including AI\, computing and data science programmes and p
 ractice-led art research (Hong Kong Baptist University's Academy of Visual
  Arts promotes the scheme for practice-led and practice-based PhDs with ac
 cess to its...\n\nOrganisation: Research Grants Council (RGC) of Hong Kong
 \, with eight Hong Kong universities\nLocation: Hong Kong: City University
  of Hong Kong\, Hong Kong Baptist University\, Lingnan University\, The Ch
 inese University of Hong Kong\, The Education University of Hong Kong\, Th
 e Hong Kong Polytechnic University\, HKUST and The University of Hong Kong
 . Open to applicants of any country of origin.\nAward: Annual stipend of H
 KD 344\,400 (about USD 44\,150) plus a conference and research travel allo
 wance of HKD 14\,400 a year\, for up to three years (2026/27 rates as publ
 ished by the RGC). Some universities add top-ups: HKBU lists a HKD 40\,000
 -a-year Elite Scholar Award for three years\, a further HKD 20\,000 travel
  top-up\, four years of tuition waiver and two years of guaranteed accommo
 dation. 400 fellowships for 2027/28.\nDuration: Full-time PhD\, up to thre
 e years of fellowship funding (HKBU programmes run four years).\n\nMore: h
 ttps://cerg1.ugc.edu.hk/hkpfs/index.html?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrant
 desk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://cerg1.ugc.edu.hk/hkpfs/index.html?utm_source=artificialnouveaug
 rantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Hong Kong: City University of Hong Kong\, Hong Kong Baptist Univer
 sity\, Lingnan University\, The Chinese University of Hong Kong\, The Educ
 ation University of Hong Kong\, The Hong Kong Polytechnic University\, HKU
 ST and The University of Hong Kong. Open to applicants of any country of o
 rigin.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:acc-next-emerging-asian-artists-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261106T131942Z
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261025
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261026
SUMMARY:Deadline: 2027 ACC NEXT Emerging Asian Artists International Open C
 all (Gwangju)
DESCRIPTION:The National Asian Culture Center (ACC) in Gwangju seeks bold\,
  experimental work by emerging artists from Asia at the intersection of ar
 t and technology for its 2027 ACC NEXT exhibition. The theme is Prototype\
 ; works must not have been presented in another exhibition\, or must be re
 -created works.\n\nOrganisation: National Asian Culture Center (ACC)\nLoca
 tion: National Asian Culture Center\, Gwangju\, South Korea. Open to natio
 nals of Asian countries born on or after 1 January 1987\; artists born or 
 raised in Asia whose practice deeply engages with Asian identities may als
 o be considered regardless of nationality.\nAward: Artist fee of KRW 3\,00
 0\,000 per work\, an installation and materials budget of up to KRW 2\,000
 \,000 per work\, one round-trip international airfare (or domestic transpo
 rtation)\, and tentative accommodation at Asia Plex Studio. One artist or 
 team is additionally selected for the 2027 ACC CREATORS Residency through 
 an artist pitch review. For teams\, fees\, travel and accommodation go to 
 the team leader only.\nDuration: Exhibition of selected works at ACC in 20
 27\; selected artists must attend the installation\, opening and artist pi
 tch\n\nMore: https://www.acc.go.kr/en/board/board.do?PID=1001&boardID=NOTI
 CE&action=Read&idx=2866&utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=r
 eferral
URL:https://www.acc.go.kr/en/board/board.do?PID=1001&boardID=NOTICE&action=
 Read&idx=2866&utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:National Asian Culture Center\, Gwangju\, South Korea. Open to nat
 ionals of Asian countries born on or after 1 January 1987\; artists born o
 r raised in Asia whose practice deeply engages with Asian identities may a
 lso be considered regardless of nationality.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:alkazi-curatorial-research-fellowship-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261106T131942Z
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261107
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261108
SUMMARY:Deadline: Alkazi Foundation: Curatorial Research Fellowship 2027 (w
 ith CWIT and the V&A)
DESCRIPTION:A funded research residency (3rd edition of the Visiting Curato
 rial Research Fellowship) for mid-career cultural producers from India: ar
 tists\, scholars\, writers/editors and curators pursuing humanities-driven
  research in the V&A's global photography and visual-culture collections i
 n London. The awardee is announced in February 2027 and the fellowship sta
 rts April 2027.\n\nOrganisation: Alkazi Foundation for the Arts\, with the
  Charles Wallace India Trust and the Victoria and Albert Museum\nLocation:
  New Delhi\, India (organiser)\; the funded research residency takes place
  at the V&A Photography Section\, London. RESTRICTED: Indian citizens domi
 ciled in India\, aged 25 to 45\, mid-career.\nAward: GBP 1\,600 monthly st
 ipend for 3 to 6 months\, plus a GBP 800 contribution from CWIT towards in
 ternational return airfare\; visa expenses covered by the Alkazi Foundatio
 n. No application fee.\nDuration: 3 to 6 months\n\nMore: https://alkazifou
 ndation.org/call-for-entries-5/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_
 medium=referral
URL:https://alkazifoundation.org/call-for-entries-5/?utm_source=artificialn
 ouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:New Delhi\, India (organiser)\; the funded research residency take
 s place at the V&A Photography Section\, London. RESTRICTED: Indian citize
 ns domiciled in India\, aged 25 to 45\, mid-career.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:yao-residency-02-taiwan-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261106T131942Z
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261231
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270101
SUMMARY:Deadline: YAO Residency #02 (Taiwan): Research Residency 2027 and E
 xhibition 2028
DESCRIPTION:YAO Residency #02 centres on the translation between culture an
 d material: through living\, research and exchange in Taiwan\, artists eng
 age with different cultural contexts\, local ways of living\, materials an
 d craft practices\, with emphasis on process rather than finished works. O
 NE artist/practitioner is selected for a two-phase program.\n\nOrganisatio
 n: YAO Residency Program (Yao Zuo Zhu Cun Ji Hua)\nLocation: Taiwan. Open 
 worldwide to applicants aged 18 and above\, regardless of nationality\; in
 ternational artists arrange their own entry and visa (YAO can provide an i
 nvitation letter).\nAward: Research Residency 2027: travel support (intern
 ational applicants reimbursed up to NTD 20\,000 for one round-trip to Taiw
 an against receipts)\, production budget up to NTD 20\,000\, living stipen
 d of NTD 10\,000\, accommodation\, Open Studio venue\, local connections\,
  and documentation\, text editing\, translation and promotional support. E
 xhibition Phase 2028: travel support up to NTD 20\,000 again\, a further N
 TD 10\,000 living stipend\, accommodation\, exhibition venue at YAO\, inst
 allation and de-installation assistance\, and exhibition documentation. Ap
 plication fee: NTD 300 for Taiwan-based applicants (bank transfer) or USD 
 10 for international applicants (PayPal)\, non-refundable.\nDuration: Two 
 phases: research residency 21 August to 21 November 2027 with Open Studio 
 27 October to 16 November 2027\, then a formal exhibition at YAO in 2028 (
 expected to run at least six weeks\, dates agreed with the artist). The se
 lected artist commits to both phases.\n\nMore: https://docs.google.com/for
 ms/d/e/1FAIpQLSfQ5-RBrfPckf4O9A5LeDrAzbFlXHzBkYrpPyTiy3HeKc8BkQ/viewform?u
 tm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSfQ5-RBrfPckf4O9A5LeDrAzbFlXHz
 BkYrpPyTiy3HeKc8BkQ/viewform?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_med
 ium=referral
LOCATION:Taiwan. Open worldwide to applicants aged 18 and above\, regardles
 s of nationality\; international artists arrange their own entry and visa 
 (YAO can provide an invitation letter).
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:tarbell-fellowship-2027-28@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261106T131942Z
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261122
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261123
SUMMARY:Deadline: Tarbell Fellowship 2027-28 (AI journalism)
DESCRIPTION:A year-long fellowship for journalists covering artificial inte
 lligence. Fellows complete a three-month full-time remote programme on AI 
 and journalism fundamentals\, attend a weeklong summit\, then work for nin
 e months as reporters embedded in a partner newsroom (current partners are
  in Hong Kong\, London\, Los Angeles\, New York\, San Francisco\, Seattle\
 , Washington DC and Cambridge).\n\nOrganisation: Tarbell Center for AI Jou
 rnalism\nLocation: Remote training\, then newsroom placement in the US\, U
 K or Hong Kong. In person.\nAward: USD 75\,000 to 120\,000 depending on ex
 perience and placement cost of living\; senior fellows (7+ years experienc
 e) USD 115\,000 to 135\,000. Summit travel and accommodation covered. No a
 pplication fee.\nDuration: 12 months: remote training 7 June to 6 August 2
 027\, in-person summit August 2027\, newsroom placement September 2027 to 
 May 2028 (extendable by one year).\n\nMore: https://www.tarbellcenter.org/
 fellowship?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.tarbellcenter.org/fellowship?utm_source=artificialnouveaugr
 antdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Remote training\, then newsroom placement in the US\, UK or Hong K
 ong. In person.
END:VEVENT
