SUMMARY:Deadline: PARC Palestinian Research Fellowship 2027-2028 (up to USD
  6\,000\, arts\, humanities and social sciences)
DESCRIPTION:PARC's 28th annual fellowship competition for Palestinian schol
 ars funds field-based research in the arts\, humanities\, social sciences\
 , public health and environmental studies\; purely scientific research is 
 not eligible.\n\nOrganisation: Palestinian American Research Center (PARC)
 \nLocation: For Palestinian researchers regardless of residence or ID\; fi
 eldwork in Palestine\, Jordan\, Egypt or Lebanon.\nAward: Up to USD 6\,000
  per fellowship (tuition not covered). No application fee mentioned.\nDura
 tion: 2 to 12 months of fieldwork\; research to be completed by 31 Decembe
 r 2028.\n\nMore: https://www.parc-us-pal.org/fellowships-for-palestinians/
 ?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.parc-us-pal.org/fellowships-for-palestinians/?utm_source=ar
 tificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:For Palestinian researchers regardless of residence or ID\; fieldw
 ork in Palestine\, Jordan\, Egypt or Lebanon.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:daiwa-foundation-small-grants-march-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261106T131942Z
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270331
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270401
SUMMARY:Deadline: Daiwa Foundation Small Grants\, March 2027 round (GBP 2\,
 000-9\,000 for UK-Japan projects)
DESCRIPTION:The Daiwa Foundation Small Grants support projects that promote
  interaction between the UK and Japan in any field\, including arts exchan
 ges\, exhibitions\, conferences\, grassroots and educational exchanges and
  research travel\, with travel between the two countries as the main focus
 .\n\nOrganisation: Daiwa Anglo-Japanese Foundation\nLocation: For individu
 als\, societies\, associations and other bodies in the UK or Japan running
  projects that connect the two countries.\nAward: GBP 2\,000 to 9\,000 (ty
 pical awards GBP 3\,000-4\,000)\; flights up to GBP 1\,200 each and subsis
 tence up to GBP 100 per person per day. A contribution\, not full funding.
  No application fee.\nDuration: Per project\; activity can start from late
  May or early June 2027.\n\nMore: https://dajf.org.uk/grants-awards-and-pr
 izes/daiwa-foundation-small-grants?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&u
 tm_medium=referral
URL:https://dajf.org.uk/grants-awards-and-prizes/daiwa-foundation-small-gra
 nts?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:For individuals\, societies\, associations and other bodies in the
  UK or Japan running projects that connect the two countries.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:beijing-ai-safety-hub-residency-spring-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261106T131942Z
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261106
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261107
SUMMARY:Deadline: Beijing AI Safety Hub (Tsinghua): Spring 2027 AI Safety R
 esidency (USD 5\,000/month)
DESCRIPTION:A self-directed research residency at the Beijing AI Safety Hub
 \, affiliated with Tsinghua University (co-directors Soeren Mindermann and
  Prof. Xu Wei\; chief scientist Prof. Andrew Yao). Unlike structured mento
 rship programmes such as MATS or Astra\, residents bring their own researc
 h agenda.\n\nOrganisation: Beijing AI Safety Hub\, Tsinghua University\nLo
 cation: Beijing\, China. Hosted at the Beijing AI Safety Hub\; no Mandarin
  or China background needed.\nAward: USD 5\,000 per month for about three 
 months\, plus flights\, housing\, visa support and devices. No application
  fee stated.\nDuration: About three months from April 2027.\n\nMore: https
 ://lesswrong.com/posts/bgTP2SrFcTYBSwbxa/tsinghua-started-an-ai-safety-res
 idency?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://lesswrong.com/posts/bgTP2SrFcTYBSwbxa/tsinghua-started-an-ai-sa
 fety-residency?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Beijing\, China. Hosted at the Beijing AI Safety Hub\; no Mandarin
  or China background needed.
END:VEVENT
